source: crates/instrukt-cli/tests/cases/work-dispatch.rs
expression: "format!(\"outside:\\n{}---\\nunclaimed:\\n{}---\\nchild:\\n{}\",\nString::from_utf8_lossy(&outside.get_output().stderr),\nString::from_utf8_lossy(&unclaimed.get_output().stderr),\nString::from_utf8_lossy(&from_child.get_output().stderr),)"
---
outside:
instrukt: `--work-ready` requires the claim-holding orchestrator session; run it from the orchestrator holding the todo's claim
---
unclaimed:
instrukt: `guarded-stamp` holds no execution claim; claim it from the orchestrator with `instrukt todo work guarded-stamp` before recording `--work-ready`
---
child:
instrukt: only the claim-holding orchestrator may record `--work-ready` for `guarded-stamp`; run it from the session holding the claim
